  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {容疑|ようぎ}を{否認|ひにん}する (deny allegations/charges)\n- {関与|かんよ}を{否認|ひにん}する (deny involvement)\n- {全面|ぜんめん}{否認|ひにん} (complete denial)\n- {事実|じじつ}を{否認|ひにん}する (deny the facts)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{否定|ひてい} (denial, negation) is a broader term — you can deny facts, ideas, or existence. {否認|ひにん} is more specific and formal, typically used for denying accusations, charges, or responsibility. In legal contexts, {否認|ひにん} is the standard term for a defendant's denial of charges.",
